Ok. Got it! With mouse it works like a charm, but via gamepad or keyboard this can be replicated. I'll take a look at it!
EDIT:
This seems to be how RPG Maker works... If event page has ANY rows (including event comments) it will prevent events "there" trigger... But I might add plugin parameter in OcRam_Core that allows comments to equal nothing. It already includes similar changes to RMMZ core scripts.
EDIT2:
This is quick fix for this issue. (I will add new plugin parameter in next patch to enable / disable this feature - because we never know if someone wants to start events which has only comments in it...)
Code:
// Add this
this.extend(Game_Event, "start", function () {
    const list = this.list().filter(itm => itm.code != 108 && itm.code != 0);
    if (!list || list.length < 1) return;
    _this["Game_Event_start"].apply(this, arguments);
});

