Here's a fun one I never noticed since some latest patches hit:
Setting the player's Light Source to NONE as a default blanks the screen.
Setting the player's Light Source to NONE in a Common Event (Say startup) makes scene transfers blank the screen.
Leaving things as default: gives the player a 'hue' around them the size of the light radius during all hours. Inside and Out, regardless of any settings. (I run the Time System as well.)
Shutting down the light fixes the hue, but you have to manually reset the global light each transfer.
